---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config";
import { TAX_YEAR } from "../lib/paycheck-tax";

const title = "About — ByteTech247 Tools";
const description =
  "Who builds ByteTech247 Tools and why the paycheck calculator sources every figure directly from the IRS instead of guessing.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="content-page">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Built to be honest, not just convenient</h2>
      <p>
        The Paycheck Calculator exists because most take-home-pay tools online
        quietly guess. This one doesn't: federal income tax and FICA are
        computed from the actual {TAX_YEAR} IRS tax brackets and standard deduction,
        sourced directly from the IRS's own tax-year {TAX_YEAR}{" "}
        inflation-adjustment announcement. When a number can be verified against a
        primary source, it's labeled <strong>Exact</strong>. When it can't —
        most state income tax, which this tool doesn't model — it's labeled <strong
          >Estimated</strong
        >, never dressed up as fact.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who built this</h2>
      <p>
        Aboagye Annor builds and maintains ByteTech247 Tools as an independent,
        solo project. It isn't a company, and it isn't a team of CPAs or
        financial advisors — it's one person's attempt to build the kind of
        calculator they'd actually want to use themselves.
      </p>
      <p>
        That also means this site is not a financial institution, and nothing it
        calculates is professional tax or financial advice. For anything
        consequential — a big life decision, a dispute with an employer, an
        actual tax filing — verify the numbers with a CPA or the IRS directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How the numbers stay accurate</h2>
      <p>
        Federal figures are refreshed at the start of each tax year against the
        IRS's own published Revenue Procedure, not a third-party summary of it.
        If something looks wrong, that's worth reporting — see{" "}
        <a href="/contact">Contact</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What this isn't</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Not a signup — there's no account, no saved data, no email capture.
        </li>
        <li>
          Not a data collector — see the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for
          exactly what that means.
        </li>
        <li>Not professional tax or financial advice.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Part of a growing family</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is the first of a planned family of small, focused tools
        under the ByteTech247 name — each one built around a single job done honestly,
        rather than a bundle of everything at once.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
